d elements\n  - No nested structures; flat schema.\n  - No explicit edges are provided—only per-layer degree counts per agent.\n  - Implies a multiplex network with three layers (family, work/school, community); total_connections is a derived field validating degree sums.\n- How this data should inform simulation entities or interactions\n  - Agent initialization: create one agent per row with the given demographics, initial_mask_wearing state, and risk_perception trait.\n  - Network construction: generate a three-layer (family, work/school, community) graph using the provided degree sequence per layer (e.g., configuration model), enforcing that each agent’s degree matches its counts; optionally apply assortativity/homophily by age_group and occupation when pairing stubs.\n  - Interaction dynamics:\n    - Use layer-specific contacts to compute social influence (e.g., fraction of masked neighbors per layer).\n    - Weight layers differently (family > work/school > community, if desired).\n    - Update mask adoption probability as a function of risk_perception and observed neighbor masking (and optionally demographics/occupation).\n  - Validation: ensure degree sums are even per layer and total_connections equals the per-layer sum; handle missing/boolean parsing consistently.\n\nFile: social_network.json (type: json)\n\nExample data of this file: \n{\'0\': {\'family\': [80, 500, 122], \'work_school\': [1, 998, 5, 994], \'community\': [879, 712, 900, 533, 624, 691, 69, 315, 379, 647, 847], \'all\': [80, 500, 122, 1, 998, 5, 994, 879, 712, 900, 533, 624, 691, 69, 315, 379, 647, 847]}, \'1\': {\'family\': [534, 441, 760], \'work_school\': [0, 5, 8, 998], \'community\': [729, 55, 955, 975, 453, 68, 246, 281, 400, 606, 900, 910], \'all\': [534, 441, 760, 0, 5, 8, 998, 729, 55, 955, 975, 453, 68, 246, 281, 400, 606, 900, 910]}, \'2\': {\'family\': [655, 771, 294, 206], \'work_school\': [15, 973, 49, 971, 951], \'community\': [995, 868, 780, 116, 111, 807, 630, 629, 76, 352,